(function(E){ const x = E["exam-10"] = E["exam-10"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x10-r1"] = {"id":"x10-r1","patterns":["RA-nature","GT1-reviews","GT1-notices","PARA-cause","PARA-research","PARA-rules","TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge","TR-paraphrase","TR-limit","TR-plural","TR-samewords","TR-whosevoice"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a natural-history passage, watching for words like always and many, and then complete notes with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir doğa tarihi metninde always ve many gibi kelimelere dikkat ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi, sonra notları metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی متنی از تاریخ طبیعی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و حواست به کلمه‌هایی مثل always و many باشد، و بعد یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match features to the right business in a set of short reviews, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a council notice.","tr":"Bu derste kısa yorumlarda özellikleri doğru işletmeyle eşleştirmeyi ve bir belediye duyurusunda TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری در مجموعه‌ای از نظرهای کوتاه، ویژگی‌ها را با کسب‌وکار درست جور کنی و درباره‌ی اطلاعیه‌ی شهرداری بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: nature and climate","tr":"Reading Passage 1: doğa ve iklim","fa":"Reading Passage 1: طبیعت و اقلیم"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a natural-history passage, watching for words like always and many, and then complete notes with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir doğa tarihi metninde always ve many gibi kelimelere dikkat ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi, sonra notları metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی متنی از تاریخ طبیعی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و حواست به کلمه‌هایی مثل always و many باشد، و بعد یادداشت‌ها را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~780"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: bumblebees in winter","tr":"Bu sınav: kışın bombus arıları","fa":"این آزمون: زنبورهای درشت در زمستان"},"intro":{"en":"Animals, plants and ecosystems are the largest family of Academic topics. Passage 1 usually explains how something normally works before describing a change, so the first paragraphs give you the background for the statements.","tr":"Hayvanlar, bitkiler ve ekosistemler en büyük Academic konu ailesidir. Passage 1 genelde bir değişimi anlatmadan önce bir şeyin normalde nasıl işlediğini açıklar; ilk paragraflar ifadeler için arka planı verir.","fa":"جانوران، گیاهان و زیست‌بوم‌ها بزرگ‌ترین خانواده‌ی موضوع‌های Academic هستند. Passage 1 معمولاً قبل از توصیف یک تغییر توضیح می‌دهد چیزی در حالت عادی چطور کار می‌کند، پس پاراگراف‌های اول زمینه‌ی جمله‌ها را می‌دهند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x10-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An animal and a changing climate","tr":"Bir hayvan ve değişen iklim","fa":"یک جانور و اقلیم در حال تغییر"},"asks":{"en":"A natural-history account: how an animal normally lives through the year, a new behaviour scientists have noticed, the causes, the risks, how the changes are monitored and what ordinary people can do. TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN comes first; the notes cover the later paragraphs.","tr":"Doğa tarihi anlatımı: bir hayvanın yıl boyunca normalde nasıl yaşadığı, bilim insanlarının fark ettiği yeni bir davranış, nedenleri, riskleri, değişimlerin nasıl izlendiği ve sıradan insanların ne yapabileceği. Önce TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN gelir; notlar son paragrafları kapsar.","fa":"روایتی از تاریخ طبیعی: یک جانور معمولاً چطور سال را می‌گذراند، رفتار تازه‌ای که دانشمندان دیده‌اند، علت‌ها، خطرها، اینکه تغییرها چطور زیر نظر گرفته می‌شوند و مردم عادی چه می‌توانند بکنند. اول TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN می‌آید؛ یادداشت‌ها پاراگراف‌های آخر را پوشش می‌دهند."},"fields":["The normal life cycle","A new behaviour","Why it happens","Risks","Monitoring","What people can do"],"words":[{"a":"survive the winter","b":"live through / remain until spring","tr":"kışı atlatmak","fa":"زمستان را زنده ماندن"},{"a":"die","b":"do not survive / the old queen dies","tr":"ölmek","fa":"مردن"},{"a":"underground","b":"in a hole in the soil","tr":"yer altında","fa":"زیر زمین"},{"a":"active","b":"flying / collecting pollen","tr":"etkin","fa":"فعال"},{"a":"rely on","b":"depend on","tr":"... e bağlı olmak","fa":"متکی بودن به"},{"a":"store","b":"reserves","tr":"depo, rezerv","fa":"ذخیره"},{"a":"less common","b":"declining / fewer of them","tr":"daha az yaygın","fa":"کمیاب‌تر"},{"a":"volunteers","b":"ordinary people, not professional scientists","tr":"gönüllüler","fa":"داوطلب‌ها"},{"a":"once a month","b":"every month","tr":"ayda bir","fa":"ماهی یک بار"},{"a":"many","b":"not all / some","tr":"birçok","fa":"خیلی‌ها"}],"traps":[{"en":"Absolute words: \"always\", \"never\", \"all\". If the text says \"many... do survive\", a statement with \"always die\" is FALSE.","tr":"Kesin kelimeler: \"always\", \"never\", \"all\". Metin \"birçoğu... hayatta kalıyor\" diyorsa \"her zaman ölür\" diyen ifade FALSE’tur.","fa":"کلمه‌های مطلق: «always»، «never»، «all». اگر متن می‌گوید «خیلی‌ها... زنده می‌مانند»، جمله‌ای با «همیشه می‌میرند» FALSE است."},{"en":"A place or group that is not mentioned: \"places, especially towns\" says nothing about other countries. That is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Söz edilmeyen bir yer ya da grup: \"yerler, özellikle kasabalar\" başka ülkeler hakkında bir şey söylemez. Bu NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"جا یا گروهی که اسمش نیامده: «جاها، به‌خصوص شهرها» درباره‌ی کشورهای دیگر چیزی نمی‌گوید. این NOT GIVEN است."}],"example":{"text":"\"Most swallows leave in September, although a few stay until October.\"","item":"Statement: All swallows leave by the end of September.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"A few stay until October\" contradicts \"all... by the end of September\".","tr":"\"Birkaçı ekime kadar kalıyor\", \"hepsi eylül sonuna kadar\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«چندتایی تا اکتبر می‌مانند» با «همه... تا آخر سپتامبر» تناقض دارد."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-p1","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Natural history accounts","tr":"Doğa tarihi anlatıları","fa":"روایت‌های تاریخ طبیعی"},"asks":{"en":"A factual account of an animal, a plant or a natural place: how it lives, how it was discovered, why it declined and how it is protected. Statements test single facts; the notes follow the order of the text.","tr":"Bir hayvan, bitki ya da doğal bir yer hakkında bilgilendirici bir metin: nasıl yaşadığı, nasıl keşfedildiği, neden azaldığı ve nasıl korunduğu. İfadeler tek tek bilgileri sınar; notlar metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"متنی اطلاعاتی درباره‌ی یک حیوان، یک گیاه یا یک مکان طبیعی: چطور زندگی می‌کند، چطور کشف شد، چرا کم شد و چطور از آن حفاظت می‌شود. جمله‌ها اطلاعات جزئی را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The species was first described in the 1800s.","Its numbers have fallen since the 1950s.","It is found only on one island.","Farmers consider it a pest.","Notes: Diet · Habitat · Threats · Protection"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"fell in number / became scarcer","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"disappeared","b":"became extinct / died out","tr":"yok oldu","fa":"از بین رفت"},{"a":"only","b":"exclusively / nowhere else","tr":"yalnızca","fa":"فقط"},{"a":"first","b":"the earliest / originally","tr":"ilk","fa":"اولین"},{"a":"increased","b":"rose / grew / expanded","tr":"arttı","fa":"افزایش یافت"},{"a":"protect","b":"conserve / save from","tr":"korumak","fa":"حفاظت کردن"},{"a":"harmful","b":"damaging / a threat to","tr":"zararlı","fa":"مضر"},{"a":"common","b":"widespread / found in many places","tr":"yaygın","fa":"رایج"},{"a":"scientists","b":"researchers / biologists","tr":"bilim insanları","fa":"دانشمندان"},{"a":"uncertain","b":"it remains unclear / not yet known","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"caused by","b":"the result of / due to","tr":"... yüzünden","fa":"ناشی از"},{"a":"brought in","b":"introduced by humans","tr":"dışarıdan getirilmiş","fa":"وارد شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Hedging: \"may\", \"some researchers believe\". A statement that turns this into a fact is usually FALSE or NOT GIVEN; compare carefully.","tr":"Temkinli dil: \"may\", \"bazı araştırmacılara göre\". Bunu kesin bilgiye çeviren bir ifade genelde FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olur; dikkatle karşılaştır.","fa":"زبان محتاطانه: «may»، «بعضی پژوهشگرها معتقدند». جمله‌ای که این را به واقعیت قطعی تبدیل کند معمولاً FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است؛ دقیق مقایسه کن."},{"en":"\"Only\", \"always\", \"never\" in a statement: one exception in the text makes it FALSE.","tr":"İfadede \"only\", \"always\", \"never\": metindeki tek bir istisna onu FALSE yapar.","fa":"«only»، «always»، «never» در جمله: یک استثنا در متن آن را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Notes: two numbers or dates sit close together. The heading decides which one you need.","tr":"Notlar: iki sayı ya da tarih yan yanadır. Hangisinin gerektiğine başlık karar verir.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها: دو عدد یا تاریخ نزدیک هم‌اند. عنوان تعیین می‌کند کدام را لازم داری."}],"example":{"text":"The hazel dormouse was once found in woods across most of England. Its range has shrunk by about half since 1900, mainly because the hedges that linked woodlands were removed. Most surviving populations are now in the south.","item":"Statement: The dormouse has always lived only in the south of England.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Once found in woods across most of England\" contradicts \"always... only in the south\".","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar İngiltere’nin çoğunda\" bulunması, \"her zaman... yalnızca güneyde\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«زمانی در جنگل‌های بیشتر انگلستان بود» با «همیشه... فقط در جنوب» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Six statements, then seven notes","tr":"Altı ifade, sonra yedi not","fa":"شش جمله، بعد هفت یادداشت"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-6: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Questions 7-13: complete notes with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Both sets follow the passage order, and the notes cover the second half.","tr":"Soru 1-6: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 7-13: notları metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. İki grup da metnin sırasını izler; notlar ikinci yarıyı kapsar.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۶: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN. سؤال‌های ۷ تا ۱۳: یادداشت‌ها را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. هر دو گروه به ترتیب متن‌اند و یادداشت‌ها نیمه‌ی دوم را پوشش می‌دهند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline the subject of each statement (queens, males, winter colonies) and find where the passage discusses it.","tr":"Her ifadenin öznesinin (kraliçeler, erkekler, kış kolonileri) altını çiz ve metnin onu nerede anlattığını bul.","fa":"زیر فاعل هر جمله (ملکه‌ها، نرها، کلونی‌های زمستانی) خط بکش و پیدا کن متن کجا درباره‌اش حرف می‌زند."},{"en":"Circle absolute and limiting words: always, all, only, many, partly.","tr":"Kesin ve sınırlayıcı kelimeleri daire içine al: always, all, only, many, partly.","fa":"دور کلمه‌های مطلق و محدودکننده خط بکش: always، all، only، many، partly."},{"en":"Decide: same meaning, opposite, or not mentioned at all.","tr":"Karar ver: aynı anlam, tersi ya da hiç söz edilmemiş.","fa":"تصمیم بگیر: همان معنی، برعکس، یا اصلاً گفته نشده."},{"en":"For the notes, use the headings to find the paragraph, then copy one word exactly.","tr":"Notlar için başlıklarla paragrafı bul, sonra tek kelimeyi aynen kopyala.","fa":"برای یادداشت‌ها با کمک عنوان‌ها پاراگراف را پیدا کن و بعد یک کلمه را دقیق کپی کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"Hedgehogs sleep through the winter in nests of leaves. Some wake briefly during mild spells to look for food.\"","item":"Statement: Hedgehogs never wake up during the winter.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: \"sleep through the winter... Some wake briefly\".","tr":"Yeri bul: \"kışı uyuyarak geçirirler... Bazıları kısa süre uyanır\".","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: «زمستان را می‌خوابند... بعضی‌ها کوتاه بیدار می‌شوند»."},{"en":"Compare: \"some wake\" against \"never wake\".","tr":"Karşılaştır: \"bazıları uyanır\" ile \"asla uyanmazlar\".","fa":"مقایسه کن: «بعضی‌ها بیدار می‌شوند» در برابر «هرگز بیدار نمی‌شوند»."},{"en":"The text contradicts \"never\": FALSE.","tr":"Metin \"never\" ile çelişiyor: FALSE.","fa":"متن با «never» تناقض دارد: FALSE."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Frogs lay their eggs in ponds and slow streams.\" Statement: \"Frogs lay more eggs in ponds than in streams.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Both places are mentioned, but there is no comparison of numbers.","tr":"İki yerden de söz ediliyor ama sayılar karşılaştırılmıyor.","fa":"از هر دو جا حرف زده شده، اما تعدادها مقایسه نشده‌اند."}},"remember":{"en":"Watch absolute words; a detail the text never compares or names is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Kesin kelimelere dikkat et; metnin hiç karşılaştırmadığı ya da adını anmadığı bir ayrıntı NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"حواست به کلمه‌های مطلق باشد؛ جزئیاتی که متن هرگز مقایسه نکرده یا اسمش را نیاورده NOT GIVEN است."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x10-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-10","unit":"x10-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"Bumblebees and the changing winter","tr":"Bombus arıları ve değişen kış","fa":"زنبورهای درشت و زمستانِ در حال تغییر"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"Bumblebees and the changing winter\n\nWith their round, furry bodies and slow, heavy flight, bumblebees are among the most familiar insects in gardens across northern Europe. They are also among the most important. Bumblebees pollinate many wild flowers and a large number of crops, from tomatoes to strawberries, and they can work in cool, cloudy weather when many other insects stay at home. Some crops, such as tomatoes grown in greenhouses, release their pollen only when a bee vibrates the flower at a particular frequency, a technique at which bumblebees are especially skilled. Yet in recent decades scientists have noticed something unexpected: in some places, bumblebees are now flying in the middle of winter.\n\nTo understand why this is surprising, it helps to know how a bumblebee colony normally works. Unlike honeybees, which live through the winter as a large group inside the hive, most bumblebee colonies last for only a single summer. In late summer the colony produces new queens and males. The males die in the autumn, along with the old queen and the workers, and only the young, mated queens survive. Each one finds a sheltered spot, often a small hole in the soil or under a pile of leaves, and remains there in a deep sleep until the following spring. When the weather warms up, she wakes, feeds on the first flowers of the year and looks for a suitable nest site, where she lays her first eggs and raises a small group of workers by herself.\n\nIn the 1990s, however, naturalists in southern England began to report bumblebees collecting pollen in December and January. Further observations showed that these were not lost individuals but whole colonies, with workers flying on mild days. Some queens, it seemed, were no longer sleeping through the winter but starting new colonies straight away. This behaviour has since been recorded in a growing number of places, especially in towns, where temperatures are a little higher than in the surrounding countryside.\n\nWinter-active bees face an obvious problem: there are very few wild flowers in bloom at that time of year. Their survival appears to depend largely on plants that people grow in parks and gardens, including winter-flowering shrubs brought from other parts of the world. In one city park, observers counted more bumblebees on a single flowering bush in January than on all the native plants nearby. In this sense, the change is not only a result of warmer weather but also of the way people have altered the landscape.\n\nWarmer winters affect sleeping queens too. A queen survives the winter on the fat she has stored in her body, and a mild spell can wake her too early. If she emerges before flowers are available, she may use up her reserves of fat before she can find any food. Many queens that wake early do survive, especially in gardens, but each false start reduces her chances of founding a strong colony. A sudden frost after a warm week can be particularly dangerous, because a queen that has left her shelter may not be able to find another one in time.\n\nSummer heat brings a different risk. A bumblebee's thick fur, so useful on a cold morning, makes it difficult for the insect to lose heat on a very hot day. Studies of museum collections and long-term records suggest that several species have become less common at the southern edge of their range, while being found further north than before. In mountain regions, some species are now found only at higher altitudes than they were fifty years ago.\n\nMuch of what is known about these changes comes not from professional scientists but from volunteers. In several countries, thousands of people take part in schemes in which they walk the same route once a month and record every bumblebee they see. For each one, they note the species and, where possible, whether it is a queen, a worker or a male. Because the counts are repeated on the same route year after year, they show how the number of bees changes over time, as well as which species are becoming more or less common.\n\nResearchers are cautious about what the winter activity means. Some see it as a sign of how adaptable bumblebees are; others worry that it may make colonies more vulnerable to sudden cold spells. What is clear is that ordinary gardeners can make a difference. Planting flowers that bloom in early spring, as well as late in the year, gives both sleeping and active queens a better chance of finding food when they need it most, and leaving some areas of the garden untidy provides places for them to rest.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-6. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Young bumblebee queens usually spend the winter under the ground or under leaves.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"often a small hole in the soil or under a pile of leaves","why":{"en":"\"A small hole in the soil or under a pile of leaves\" = under the ground or under leaves.","tr":"\"Toprakta küçük bir delik ya da bir yaprak yığınının altı\".","fa":"«سوراخی کوچک در خاک یا زیر توده‌ای از برگ»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Male bumblebees survive the winter together with the queens.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"The males die in the autumn","why":{"en":"\"The males die in the autumn\"; only the young queens survive.","tr":"\"Erkekler sonbaharda ölür\"; yalnızca genç kraliçeler hayatta kalır.","fa":"«نرها در پاییز می‌میرند»؛ فقط ملکه‌های جوان زنده می‌مانند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Winter-active colonies have now been found in several other countries.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"This behaviour has since been recorded in a growing number of places","why":{"en":"The text says \"a growing number of places, especially in towns\", but it never mentions other countries.","tr":"Metin \"giderek artan sayıda yerde, özellikle kasabalarda\" diyor ama başka ülkelerden hiç söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید «در جاهای روزافزونی، به‌خصوص شهرها»، اما هیچ‌وقت از کشورهای دیگر حرف نمی‌زند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Bees that are active in winter rely heavily on plants grown by people.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Their survival appears to depend largely on plants that people grow in parks and gardens","why":{"en":"\"Appears to depend largely on plants that people grow\": rely heavily = depend largely.","tr":"\"Büyük ölçüde insanların yetiştirdiği bitkilere bağlı görünüyor\".","fa":"«به نظر می‌رسد تا حد زیادی به گیاهانی وابسته‌اند که مردم می‌کارند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-hedge"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"A queen that wakes up too early in the year will always die.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Many queens that wake early do survive","why":{"en":"\"Many queens that wake early do survive\" contradicts \"always die\".","tr":"\"Erken uyanan birçok kraliçe hayatta kalıyor\", \"her zaman ölür\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«خیلی از ملکه‌هایی که زود بیدار می‌شوند زنده می‌مانند» با «همیشه می‌میرند» تناقض دارد."},"trap":["TR-hedge"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Bees active in winter collect more pollen than bees in summer.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"more bumblebees on a single flowering bush in January than on all the native plants nearby","why":{"en":"The comparison in the text is between plants, not between winter and summer pollen.","tr":"Metindeki karşılaştırma bitkiler arasında; kış ve yaz poleni arasında değil.","fa":"مقایسه‌ی متن بین گیاه‌هاست، نه بین گرده‌ی زمستان و تابستان."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 7-13. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"The effects of warmer conditions on bumblebees","questions":[{"n":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Early waking · a queen may emerge before any ___ are available","accept":["flowers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"If she emerges before flowers are available","why":{"en":"\"Before flowers are available\". Plural.","tr":"\"Çiçekler ortada olmadan önce\". Çoğul.","fa":"«قبل از اینکه گلی در دسترس باشد». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":8,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Early waking · she may use up her store of ___","accept":["fat"],"limit":1,"evidence":"she may use up her reserves of fat","why":{"en":"\"Use up her reserves of fat\": store = reserves.","tr":"\"Yağ rezervlerini tüketebilir\": store = reserves.","fa":"«ذخیره‌ی چربی‌اش را تمام کند»: store یعنی reserves."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Heat · thick ___ makes it hard for bees to lose heat","accept":["fur"],"limit":1,"evidence":"A bumblebee's thick fur","why":{"en":"\"Thick fur, so useful on a cold morning\" makes it hard to lose heat.","tr":"\"Soğuk bir sabahta çok işe yarayan kalın tüyler\" ısı kaybetmeyi zorlaştırıyor.","fa":"«پوشش کرکیِ ضخیم که صبح سرد خیلی به درد می‌خورد» از دست دادن گرما را سخت می‌کند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Heat · some species are now found further ___ than before","accept":["north"],"limit":1,"evidence":"while being found further north than before","why":{"en":"\"Further north than before\"; at the southern edge they are less common.","tr":"\"Eskisinden daha kuzeyde\"; güney sınırında daha az görülüyorlar.","fa":"«شمالی‌تر از قبل»؛ در حاشیه‌ی جنوبی کمتر دیده می‌شوند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Monitoring · volunteers walk the same ___ every month","accept":["route"],"limit":1,"evidence":"walk the same route once a month","why":{"en":"\"Walk the same route once a month\": every month = once a month.","tr":"\"Ayda bir aynı güzergâhı yürümek\".","fa":"«ماهی یک بار همان مسیر را پیاده می‌روند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Monitoring · repeated counts show changes in the ___ of bees","accept":["number"],"limit":1,"evidence":"they show how the number of bees changes over time","why":{"en":"\"How the number of bees changes over time\".","tr":"\"Arı sayısının zamanla nasıl değiştiği\".","fa":"«تعداد زنبورها در طول زمان چطور تغییر می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Helping bees · plant flowers that bloom in early ___","accept":["spring"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Planting flowers that bloom in early spring","why":{"en":"\"Flowers that bloom in early spring, as well as late in the year\".","tr":"\"Erken ilkbaharda ve yılın sonlarında açan çiçekler\".","fa":"«گل‌هایی که اوایل بهار و همین‌طور آخر سال گل می‌دهند»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x10-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-10","unit":"x10-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"She may use up her reserves of fat.\" Reserves are...","options":["new supplies","amounts kept for later use","waste products"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Reserves = a store kept to use when needed.","tr":"Reserves = gerektiğinde kullanılmak üzere saklanan stok.","fa":"reserves یعنی ذخیره‌ای که برای وقت نیاز نگه داشته می‌شود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A note says \"every month\". Which phrase in a passage means the same?","options":["once a month","every few months","in the middle of the month"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Once a month = every month.","tr":"Once a month = her ay.","fa":"once a month یعنی هر ماه."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A statement contains the word \"always\". What should you check in the text?","options":["whether the text uses the word always","how long the paragraph is","whether the text allows any exceptions"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"If the text mentions exceptions (\"many survive\"), a statement with \"always\" is FALSE.","tr":"Metin istisnalardan söz ediyorsa (\"birçoğu hayatta kalıyor\"), \"always\" içeren ifade FALSE’tur.","fa":"اگر متن از استثنا حرف بزند («خیلی‌ها زنده می‌مانند»)، جمله‌ای با «always» FALSE است."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Owls have been seen hunting in daylight in several parks.\" Statement: \"Owls hunt in daylight in every city.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Several parks\" says nothing about every city; the text gives no information on that.","tr":"\"Birkaç park\" her şehir hakkında bir şey söylemiyor; metin bu konuda bilgi vermiyor.","fa":"«چند پارک» درباره‌ی همه‌ی شهرها چیزی نمی‌گوید؛ متن در این باره اطلاعاتی نمی‌دهد."}}],"id":"c-x10-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-10","unit":"x10-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: reviews and a notice","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: yorumlar ve bir duyuru","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: نظرها و یک اطلاعیه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match features to the right business in a set of short reviews, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a council notice.","tr":"Bu derste kısa yorumlarda özellikleri doğru işletmeyle eşleştirmeyi ve bir belediye duyurusunda TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری در مجموعه‌ای از نظرهای کوتاه، ویژگی‌ها را با کسب‌وکار درست جور کنی و درباره‌ی اطلاعیه‌ی شهرداری بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"about 20 min","tr":"yaklaşık 20 dk","fa":"حدود ۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: bakeries and a new library","tr":"Bu sınav: fırınlar ve yeni bir kütüphane","fa":"این آزمون: نانوایی‌ها و یک کتابخانه‌ی تازه"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 1 often pairs a set of reviews or listings with an official notice. The reviews test quick matching; the notice tests careful reading of plans, dates and conditions.","tr":"GT Section 1 çoğu zaman bir dizi yorum ya da listeyi resmî bir duyuruyla eşleştirir. Yorumlar hızlı eşleştirmeyi, duyuru ise planların, tarihlerin ve koşulların dikkatli okunmasını ölçer.","fa":"GT Section 1 اغلب مجموعه‌ای از نظرها یا فهرست‌ها را با یک اطلاعیه‌ی رسمی همراه می‌کند. نظرها جور کردن سریع را می‌سنجند و اطلاعیه خواندن دقیق برنامه‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و شرط‌ها را."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x10-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews","GT1-notices","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Local reviews and a council notice","tr":"Yerel yorumlar ve bir belediye duyurusu","fa":"نظرهای محلی و یک اطلاعیه‌ی شهرداری"},"asks":{"en":"First, six short reviews of local businesses, A-F: you match each feature to one business. Then a council notice about a planned building: where, what, when, how it is paid for and how to comment. You decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Önce yerel işletmeler hakkında A-F harfli altı kısa yorum: her özelliği bir işletmeyle eşleştiriyorsun. Sonra planlanan bir bina hakkında belediye duyurusu: nerede, ne, ne zaman, nasıl finanse ediliyor ve nasıl yorum yapılır. TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar veriyorsun.","fa":"اول شش نظر کوتاه درباره‌ی کسب‌وکارهای محلی با حرف A تا F: هر ویژگی را با یکی جور می‌کنی. بعد اطلاعیه‌ی شهرداری درباره‌ی یک ساختمان در دست برنامه: کجا، چه، کی، هزینه‌اش از کجا و چطور نظر بدهی. بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم می‌گیری."},"fields":["Opening times","Seating","Special products","Queues","Classes","Site","Facilities","Timing","Funding","How to comment"],"words":[{"a":"opens earlier","b":"an hour before anywhere else","tr":"daha erken açılır","fa":"زودتر باز می‌شود"},{"a":"outside","b":"on the pavement / in the garden","tr":"dışarıda","fa":"بیرون"},{"a":"without wheat","b":"made from other grains","tr":"buğdaysız","fa":"بدون گندم"},{"a":"busy","b":"the line stretches down the street","tr":"kalabalık","fa":"شلوغ"},{"a":"learn","b":"workshops / classes","tr":"öğrenmek","fa":"یاد گرفتن"},{"a":"where ... used to be","b":"on the site of the former","tr":"eskiden ... olan yerde","fa":"جایی که قبلاً ... بود"},{"a":"has decided","b":"a final decision has been made","tr":"karar verdi","fa":"تصمیم گرفته"},{"a":"expected to begin","b":"should start / is planned for","tr":"başlaması bekleniyor","fa":"انتظار می‌رود شروع شود"},{"a":"partly","b":"not the whole cost / together with","tr":"kısmen","fa":"تا حدی"},{"a":"grant","b":"money given for a project","tr":"hibe","fa":"کمک‌هزینه"},{"a":"online","b":"on the council website","tr":"çevrimiçi","fa":"آنلاین"},{"a":"believes","b":"thinks / expects","tr":"inanıyor","fa":"معتقد است"}],"traps":[{"en":"In matching features, a review can mention the right topic negatively: \"there is nowhere to sit\" does not match \"customers can sit outside\".","tr":"Özellik eşleştirmede bir yorum doğru konudan olumsuz söz edebilir: \"oturacak yer yok\", \"müşteriler dışarıda oturabilir\" ile eşleşmez.","fa":"در جور کردن ویژگی‌ها، ممکن است نظری از همان موضوع اما منفی حرف بزند: «جایی برای نشستن نیست» با «مشتری‌ها می‌توانند بیرون بنشینند» جور نیست."},{"en":"\"No decision has yet been made\" contradicts \"has decided\": that is FALSE, not NOT GIVEN.","tr":"\"Henüz bir karar verilmedi\", \"karar verdi\" ile çelişir: bu NOT GIVEN değil, FALSE’tur.","fa":"«هنوز تصمیمی گرفته نشده» با «تصمیم گرفته است» تناقض دارد: این FALSE است، نه NOT GIVEN."}],"example":{"text":"Notice: \"The pool will be open until 9 pm on weekdays.\"","item":"Statement: The pool will be open late on Saturdays.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","why":{"en":"Only weekdays are mentioned; the notice says nothing about Saturdays.","tr":"Yalnızca hafta içinden söz ediliyor; duyuru cumartesi hakkında hiçbir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"فقط روزهای کاری گفته شده؛ اطلاعیه درباره‌ی شنبه چیزی نمی‌گوید."}}},{"id":"GT1-reviews","ctx":["GT1-reviews"],"title":{"en":"Product and service reviews","tr":"Ürün ve hizmet değerlendirmeleri","fa":"نقد و معرفی کالا و خدمات"},"asks":{"en":"Short reviews or descriptions A-F of products or places: sleeping bags, kitchen machines, cafes, hotels, phone apps. Questions ask which one has a feature, or which review says something.","tr":"Ürünler ya da yerler hakkında A-F harfli kısa değerlendirmeler veya tanıtımlar: uyku tulumları, mutfak aletleri, kafeler, oteller, telefon uygulamaları. Sorular hangisinin bir özelliği olduğunu ya da hangi yorumun bir şey söylediğini sorar.","fa":"نقدها یا معرفی‌های کوتاه A تا F درباره‌ی کالاها یا مکان‌ها: کیسه‌خواب، وسایل آشپزخانه، کافه، هتل، اپلیکیشن. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام یک ویژگی را دارد، یا کدام نقد چیزی را می‌گوید."},"fields":["Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","Which cafe has outdoor seating?","Which app works without the internet?","Which hotel is suitable for families?"],"words":[{"a":"lightweight","b":"weighs very little / easy to carry","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"},{"a":"durable","b":"lasts for years / hard-wearing","tr":"dayanıklı","fa":"بادوام"},{"a":"value for money","b":"a good price for what you get","tr":"fiyatına değer","fa":"به‌صرفه"},{"a":"noisy","b":"loud","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"},{"a":"spacious","b":"lots of room","tr":"ferah","fa":"جادار"},{"a":"easy to clean","b":"wipes clean","tr":"kolay temizlenir","fa":"راحت تمیز می‌شود"},{"a":"offline","b":"without an internet connection","tr":"çevrimdışı","fa":"آفلاین"},{"a":"outdoor seating","b":"tables outside","tr":"dışarıda oturma yeri","fa":"میز در فضای باز"},{"a":"guarantee","b":"free repairs for two years","tr":"garanti","fa":"گارانتی"},{"a":"compact","b":"small / takes up little space","tr":"küçük, kompakt","fa":"جمع‌وجور"},{"a":"fully booked","b":"no rooms left","tr":"tamamen dolu","fa":"کاملاً پر"},{"a":"suitable for families","b":"children welcome / cots available","tr":"ailelere uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Superlatives: \"the lightest\" needs a comparison with all the others, not just the word \"light\".","tr":"Üstünlük sıfatları: \"en hafif\" diğerlerinin hepsiyle karşılaştırma ister, yalnızca \"hafif\" kelimesi yetmez.","fa":"صفت عالی: «سبک‌ترین» یعنی مقایسه با همه‌ی بقیه، نه فقط کلمه‌ی «سبک»."},{"en":"A review may mention a feature only to say that it is missing.","tr":"Bir yorum bir özellikten yalnızca eksik olduğunu söylemek için bahsedebilir.","fa":"یک نقد ممکن است به ویژگی‌ای فقط اشاره کند تا بگوید ندارد."}],"example":{"text":"A  The Trekker 200 weighs 900 g and packs down small.\nB  The Summit weighs just 650 g, though it is not quite as warm.\nC  The Polar Pro is the warmest of the three, at 1.4 kg.","item":"Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Compare all three: 650 g is less than 900 g and 1.4 kg.","tr":"Üçünü de karşılaştır: 650 g, 900 g ve 1,4 kg’dan az.","fa":"هر سه را مقایسه کن: ۶۵۰ گرم از ۹۰۰ گرم و ۱٫۴ کیلو کمتر است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT1-notices","ctx":["GT1-notices"],"title":{"en":"Notices, rules and FAQs","tr":"Duyurular, kurallar ve SSS","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول"},"asks":{"en":"Notices, rules and frequently asked questions for a service: a tram, a leisure centre, a block of flats, a competition. Questions test rules, conditions, dates and exceptions.","tr":"Bir hizmet için duyurular, kurallar ve sık sorulan sorular: tramvay, spor merkezi, apartman, yarışma. Sorular kuralları, koşulları, tarihleri ve istisnaları sınar.","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول برای یک خدمت: تراموا، مرکز ورزشی، یک ساختمان مسکونی، یک مسابقه. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، شرط‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و استثناها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Passengers must buy a ticket before boarding.","Children under five travel free.","Refunds are given for delays of over 30 minutes.","Residents may leave bicycles in the hallway."],"words":[{"a":"must","b":"are required to","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"prohibited / not permitted","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"within 14 days","b":"in less than two weeks","tr":"14 gün içinde","fa":"ظرف ۱۴ روز"},{"a":"can claim","b":"are entitled to / are eligible for","tr":"talep edebilir","fa":"می‌تواند درخواست کند"},{"a":"apply","b":"submit a form","tr":"başvurmak","fa":"درخواست دادن"},{"a":"proof","b":"a receipt / evidence of","tr":"kanıt","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"residents","b":"people living in the building","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for a problem you had","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"beforehand","b":"in advance","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"except","b":"apart from / with the exception of","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"must take care of","tr":"... -den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"on request","b":"if you ask","tr":"talep üzerine","fa":"در صورت درخواست"}],"traps":[{"en":"Exceptions: \"all passengers must..., except season-ticket holders\". A statement about everyone may be FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar: \"bütün yolcular ... zorunda, abonman sahipleri hariç\". Herkes hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE olabilir.","fa":"استثناها: «همه‌ی مسافران باید...، به‌جز دارندگان بلیت فصلی». جمله‌ای درباره‌ی همه ممکن است FALSE باشد."},{"en":"Numbers in conditions: \"30 minutes or more\" and \"over 30 minutes\" are not the same.","tr":"Koşullardaki sayılar: \"30 dakika veya daha fazla\" ile \"30 dakikadan fazla\" aynı değildir.","fa":"عددها در شرط‌ها: «۳۰ دقیقه یا بیشتر» با «بیش از ۳۰ دقیقه» یکی نیست."}],"example":{"text":"Delay Repay: if your train arrives 30 minutes or more late, you can claim 50% of your ticket price. Claims must be made within 28 days of travel.","item":"Statement: Passengers can claim the full price of their ticket.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"The notice says 50%, which contradicts \"the full price\".","tr":"Duyuru %50 diyor; bu \"tam fiyat\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"اطلاعیه می‌گوید ۵۰٪، که با «قیمت کامل» در تضاد است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Five features, then nine statements","tr":"Beş özellik, sonra dokuz ifade","fa":"پنج ویژگی، بعد نه جمله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-5: match each feature to a bakery, A-F; one bakery is not used, and a letter may be used more than once. Questions 6-14: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on the notice.","tr":"Soru 1-5: her özelliği bir fırınla (A-F) eşleştir; bir fırın kullanılmaz, bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 6-14: duyuru hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۵: هر ویژگی را با یک نانوایی (A تا F) جور کن؛ یک نانوایی استفاده نمی‌شود و ممکن است یک حرف بیش از یک بار بیاید. سؤال‌های ۶ تا ۱۴: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی اطلاعیه."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the five features first, then scan the reviews for each idea.","tr":"Önce beş özelliği oku, sonra her fikir için yorumları tara.","fa":"اول پنج ویژگی را بخوان و بعد برای هر ایده نظرها را مرور کن."},{"en":"Check the review says the feature positively, not that it is missing.","tr":"Yorumun özelliği olumlu söylediğini, eksik olduğunu söylemediğini kontrol et.","fa":"مطمئن شو نظر آن ویژگی را مثبت می‌گوید، نه اینکه می‌گوید ندارد."},{"en":"For the notice, use the question headings (Where? When? How will it be paid for?) to find each answer.","tr":"Duyuru için her cevabı bulmak üzere soru başlıklarını (Nerede? Ne zaman? Nasıl ödenecek?) kullan.","fa":"برای اطلاعیه با کمک عنوان‌های سؤالی (کجا؟ کی؟ هزینه‌اش چطور؟) هر جواب را پیدا کن."},{"en":"Compare days, seasons and amounts exactly: autumn is not spring, partly is not entirely.","tr":"Günleri, mevsimleri ve miktarları tam karşılaştır: sonbahar ilkbahar değildir, kısmen tamamen değildir.","fa":"روزها، فصل‌ها و مقدارها را دقیق مقایسه کن: پاییز بهار نیست، تا حدی یعنی کاملاً نیست."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Partly, not yet, only","tr":"Kısmen, henüz değil, yalnızca","fa":"تا حدی، هنوز نه، فقط"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The notice","The statement","Answer"],"tr":["Duyuru","İfade","Cevap"],"fa":["اطلاعیه","جمله","جواب"]},"rows":[["funded partly by a grant","the council pays the whole cost","FALSE"],["no decision yet","the council has decided","FALSE"],["open until 8 pm on weekdays","open on Sundays","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One feature, step by step","tr":"Bir özellik, adım adım","fa":"یک ویژگی، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Which café has the following feature?","text":"A \"Cosy, but you can’t bring dogs inside.\" B \"Our dog always gets a biscuit at the counter here.\"","item":"Feature: It welcomes dogs.","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"The feature is positive: dogs are welcome.","tr":"Özellik olumlu: köpekler hoş karşılanıyor.","fa":"ویژگی مثبت است: سگ‌ها پذیرفته می‌شوند."},{"en":"A mentions dogs, but they cannot come in: the opposite.","tr":"A köpeklerden söz ediyor ama içeri giremiyorlar: tam tersi.","fa":"A از سگ حرف می‌زند، اما نمی‌توانند داخل شوند: برعکس."},{"en":"B: the dog gets a biscuit, so dogs are welcome: B.","tr":"B: köpeğe bisküvi veriliyor, yani köpekler hoş karşılanıyor: B.","fa":"B: به سگ بیسکویت می‌دهند، پس سگ‌ها پذیرفته می‌شوند: B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Notice: \"The work is expected to take about a year.\" Statement: \"The work will definitely be finished within twelve months.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Expected... about a year\" is an estimate; it does not say the work will definitely finish in time, nor that it will not.","tr":"\"Yaklaşık bir yıl sürmesi bekleniyor\" bir tahmin; işin kesinlikle zamanında biteceğini de bitmeyeceğini de söylemiyor.","fa":"«انتظار می‌رود حدود یک سال طول بکشد» یک تخمین است؛ نه می‌گوید حتماً سر وقت تمام می‌شود و نه می‌گوید نمی‌شود."}},"remember":{"en":"Match positive features, and compare every condition in the notice exactly.","tr":"Olumlu özellikleri eşleştir ve duyurudaki her koşulu tam karşılaştır.","fa":"ویژگی‌های مثبت را جور کن و هر شرط اطلاعیه را دقیق مقایسه کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x10-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-10","unit":"x10-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"Bakeries and a new library","tr":"Fırınlar ve yeni bir kütüphane","fa":"نانوایی‌ها و یک کتابخانه‌ی تازه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-reviews","GT1-notices"],"texts":[{"title":"Westbrook bakeries: our readers’ favourites","kind":"reviews","body":"A  Hartley's Bakery\nA traditional family bakery on the High Street. The bread is excellent, and the doors open at six every morning, an hour before anywhere else in town, which makes it popular with people on their way to work. Inside, it is small and there is nowhere to sit, but the staff are quick and you rarely wait long.\n\nB  The Flour Mill\nFamous for its sourdough and cinnamon rolls. On Saturday and Sunday mornings the line of customers often stretches down the street, so go during the week if you can. Prices are a little higher than elsewhere, but most people think it is worth it.\n\nC  Little Oven\nA small café-bakery near the park, with a few tables on the pavement outside where you can sit in the sun with a coffee and a pastry. The cakes are homemade, though the choice of bread is limited.\n\nD  Rise and Shine\nGood, simple bread at low prices, and friendly staff. It is part of a small chain, so the shop itself is rather plain. Ideal if you want an ordinary loaf without spending much, and the sandwiches at lunchtime are good value too.\n\nE  Golden Crust\nThe best choice for anyone who cannot eat wheat. Around half of the loaves here are made from other grains, and the staff can tell you exactly what goes into each one. The rye bread is particularly good, and it stays fresh for several days.\n\nF  The Corner Loaf\nAs well as selling bread and cakes, the owners run evening workshops in the kitchen behind the shop, where you can learn to make your own bread or pizza. Places on the workshops fill up quickly, so book well ahead."},{"title":"Westbrook Council: plans for a new library and community hub","kind":"council notice","body":"Westbrook Council is planning to replace the town library with a new library and community hub. We would like to hear your views before a final decision is made.\n\nWhere will it be?\nThe new building will stand on the site of the former swimming pool on Station Road, which has been empty since the new leisure centre opened. The site is close to the bus station and the main car park.\n\nWhat will it include?\nAs well as a larger library with a dedicated children's area, the hub will include rooms that local groups can book for meetings, a small café and an exhibition space for local artists. Computers with free internet access will be available to all members. Opening hours will be longer than at present, with the building open until 8 pm on weekdays.\n\nWhat will happen to the current library?\nThe existing library on Church Lane will stay open until the new building is ready. No decision has yet been made about the future of the old building, and the council will consult residents separately on this question.\n\nWhen will it be built?\nIf the plans are approved, building work is expected to begin in the autumn and to take around eighteen months.\n\nHow will it be paid for?\nThe project will be funded partly by the council and partly by a national grant for community buildings, which the council was awarded last year.\n\nWhy is the council doing this?\nThe current library is too small, expensive to heat and difficult to reach for people with limited mobility. The council believes that a modern hub, with longer opening hours and a café, will attract more young people and families, who rarely use the library at present.\n\nHow can I give my views?\nYou can comment on the plans on the council website until 30 April, or attend one of two public meetings at the Town Hall. Printed copies of the plans are available at the current library."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-5. Look at the following features (Questions 1-5) and the list of bakeries below. Match each feature with the correct bakery, A-F. Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Hartley's Bakery","B The Flour Mill","C Little Oven","D Rise and Shine","E Golden Crust","F The Corner Loaf"],"questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"match","prompt":"Customers can sit outside.","correct":2,"evidence":"a few tables on the pavement outside","why":{"en":"C: \"a few tables on the pavement outside\". A has \"nowhere to sit\".","tr":"C: \"dışarıda kaldırımda birkaç masa\". A’da \"oturacak yer yok\".","fa":"C: «چند میز روی پیاده‌رو بیرون». A «جایی برای نشستن ندارد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-samewords"]},{"n":2,"kind":"match","prompt":"It opens before the other bakeries.","correct":0,"evidence":"an hour before anywhere else in town","why":{"en":"A opens at six, \"an hour before anywhere else in town\".","tr":"A saat altıda açılıyor, \"kasabadaki her yerden bir saat önce\".","fa":"A ساعت شش باز می‌شود، «یک ساعت زودتر از هر جای دیگر شهر»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"match","prompt":"It sells a large range of bread made without wheat.","correct":4,"evidence":"Around half of the loaves here are made from other grains","why":{"en":"E: \"around half of the loaves... are made from other grains\" for people who cannot eat wheat.","tr":"E: buğday yiyemeyenler için \"ekmeklerin yaklaşık yarısı... başka tahıllardan yapılıyor\".","fa":"E: برای کسانی که نمی‌توانند گندم بخورند، «حدود نیمی از نان‌ها... از غلات دیگر ساخته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is very busy at weekends.","correct":1,"evidence":"On Saturday and Sunday mornings the line of customers often stretches down the street","why":{"en":"B: on Saturday and Sunday the queue \"stretches down the street\".","tr":"B: cumartesi ve pazar sıra \"sokak boyunca uzanıyor\".","fa":"B: شنبه و یکشنبه صف «تا پایین خیابان کشیده می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"match","prompt":"You can learn to bake there.","correct":5,"evidence":"where you can learn to make your own bread or pizza","why":{"en":"F runs \"evening workshops... where you can learn to make your own bread\".","tr":"F, \"kendi ekmeğini yapmayı öğrenebileceğin akşam atölyeleri\" düzenliyor.","fa":"F «کارگاه‌های عصرانه‌ای... که در آن می‌توانی پختن نان خودت را یاد بگیری» دارد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 6-14. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The new library will be built where the old swimming pool used to be.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"on the site of the former swimming pool","why":{"en":"\"On the site of the former swimming pool\": former = used to be.","tr":"\"Eski yüzme havuzunun yerinde\".","fa":"«در محل استخر سابق»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The council has decided to sell the old library building.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"No decision has yet been made about the future of the old building","why":{"en":"\"No decision has yet been made\" contradicts \"has decided\".","tr":"\"Henüz bir karar verilmedi\", \"karar verdi\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«هنوز تصمیمی گرفته نشده» با «تصمیم گرفته است» تناقض دارد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"There will be somewhere to buy drinks in the new building.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"a small café","why":{"en":"The hub will include \"a small café\".","tr":"Merkezde \"küçük bir kafe\" olacak.","fa":"در مرکز «یک کافه‌ی کوچک» خواهد بود."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The new library will open on Sundays.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"with the building open until 8 pm on weekdays","why":{"en":"Only weekday evenings are mentioned; nothing is said about Sundays.","tr":"Yalnızca hafta içi akşamlardan söz ediliyor; pazar hakkında bir şey yok.","fa":"فقط عصرهای روزهای کاری گفته شده؛ درباره‌ی یکشنبه چیزی نیست."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Building work is expected to start in the spring.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"building work is expected to begin in the autumn","why":{"en":"Work is expected to begin \"in the autumn\".","tr":"Çalışmaların \"sonbaharda\" başlaması bekleniyor.","fa":"انتظار می‌رود کار «در پاییز» شروع شود."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The council will pay the whole cost of the project.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"funded partly by the council and partly by a national grant","why":{"en":"\"Partly by the council and partly by a national grant\", so not the whole cost.","tr":"\"Kısmen belediye, kısmen ulusal bir hibe\"; yani maliyetin tamamı değil.","fa":"«بخشی را شهرداری و بخشی را یک کمک‌هزینه‌ی ملی»، پس نه کل هزینه را."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Residents can give their opinions on the internet.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"You can comment on the plans on the council website","why":{"en":"\"Comment on the plans on the council website\" = give opinions online.","tr":"\"Belediyenin web sitesinde planlar hakkında yorum yapabilirsin\".","fa":"«می‌توانی روی سایت شهرداری درباره‌ی طرح نظر بدهی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Parking at the new site will be free of charge.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"close to the bus station and the main car park","why":{"en":"The site is near the main car park, but nothing is said about the price.","tr":"Alan ana otoparkın yakınında ama ücretten söz edilmiyor.","fa":"محل نزدیک پارکینگ اصلی است، اما درباره‌ی هزینه چیزی گفته نشده."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]},{"n":14,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The council thinks the new hub will be used by more young people.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"will attract more young people and families","why":{"en":"\"The council believes that a modern hub... will attract more young people\".","tr":"\"Belediye modern bir merkezin... daha fazla genci çekeceğine inanıyor\".","fa":"«شهرداری معتقد است یک مرکز مدرن... جوان‌های بیشتری را جذب می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-whosevoice"]}]}],"id":"c-x10-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-10","unit":"x10-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"A notice mentions a \"national grant\". A grant is...","options":["a loan that must be repaid","a type of tax","money given for a purpose"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"A grant is money given, usually by an organisation, which does not need to be paid back.","tr":"Hibe, genelde bir kurumun verdiği ve geri ödenmesi gerekmeyen paradır.","fa":"grant پولی است که معمولاً یک سازمان می‌دهد و لازم نیست پس داده شود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"on the internet\". Which words in a notice mean the same?","options":["at the Town Hall","on the council website","in printed copies"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A website is on the internet; the Town Hall and printed copies are not.","tr":"Web sitesi internettedir; belediye binası ve basılı kopyalar değil.","fa":"وب‌سایت روی اینترنت است؛ ساختمان شهرداری و نسخه‌های چاپی نه."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Five features and six bakeries (A-F). What does this tell you?","options":["At least one bakery is not used","Every bakery is used once","One feature has no answer"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Five answers from six letters: at least one letter is left over.","tr":"Altı harften beş cevap: en az bir harf artar.","fa":"پنج جواب از شش حرف: دست‌کم یک حرف می‌ماند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"The bakery has no seating inside.\" Feature: \"Customers can sit outside.\" Does this bakery match?","options":["Yes: seating is mentioned","Yes: it has no inside seating, so it must be outside","No: nothing is said about outside seating"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"No seating inside\" does not tell you there is seating outside.","tr":"\"İçeride oturma yeri yok\" dışarıda olduğunu söylemez.","fa":"«داخل جای نشستن نیست» نمی‌گوید بیرون جا هست."}}],"id":"c-x10-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-10","unit":"x10-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
